From b3107d6bb6181cc501b145b239123e671dbab9dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ericek111 <erik.brocko@letemsvetemapplem.eu>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:32:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 34/47] NMXVGAFB: flips complete at the host's latch point; VBL
 on that grid

A final (ordered) flip now flushes fenced and returns when the host has
latched the frame, so NMXAccel completes the transaction then, as a page
flip completes at vblank on real hardware. With QEMU 0007 the answers lie
on a grid (host vblank + a fixed phase), or later when a frame was drawn
after its latch point: the grid is their lower envelope. An earlier answer
moves it at once, a later one by at most 2 us (clock drift). The VBL timer
runs on that grid alone. Answers count only after 8 took over 1 ms, so a
host without 0007 (instant answers) leaves the free-running timer alone.

Measured, Safari rAF at 60 fps on the 120 Hz panel: 101 of 101 frames
held exactly two refreshes. VBL at the host's release instead (QEMU
0006's adaptive release, an earlier version of this) drifted with
WindowServer's own compositing offset; a 1.5 ms lead before the latch let
flips submitted just after a VBL catch the latch that followed it (16% of
frames uneven); debug.nmxfb_vbl_lead_us keeps that knob, default 0.

The VBL timer no longer waits on the scan-out lock a flip holds.
debug.nmxfb_vtrace lists the last 512 display events (vbl, latch, flip,
answer) for vm/tools/ftrace.sh.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
